# Grammar 16.10 / decision D-25. The rejection itself is correct: the region
# rule says an assignment anywhere in the guarded region defeats narrowing.
#
# The message is not. The program already tests `cursor != null`, so a help
# telling it to "test it with `!= null`" is advice the code has taken; nothing
# in the diagnostic mentions the assignment that actually defeated the
# narrowing, or the rule it comes from. Every other diagnostic in this compiler
# cites the rule behind it, and this is the language's sharpest edge.
code E0503
text `Node?` may be absent, so `.value` is not available
absent test it with `!= null`
